  "title": "Staying cool and chilling out",
  "summary": "“I love your country but hate the fact you have no air conditioning” was the comment that an American friend of your author shared with him when visiting London from the States recently. Some 40% of the world’s population now has access to air conditioning. However, global distribution is highly uneven, and with record temperatures being recorded across much of the planet, many probably wish they owned a unit. The politics of cooling will only become increasingly important.",
